### Findings

#### 1. [`scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh:122-187`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh#L122-L187), [`scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.lean:74-89`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.lean#L74-L89), [`scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.lean:150-185`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.lean#L150-L185) — **HIGH**
**Planted controls disable `set -e` (allowing vacuous passes when `control-emit` fails) and [`lcbOffByOne`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.lean#L74-L89) breaks LCB canonical value numbering on 4 of the 5 BIR productions.**

- **`set -e` disabled inside [`run_control`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh#L122-L132):**
  `( "$fn" ) >"$log" 2>&1 || rc=$?` ([`spec_diff.sh:124`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh#L124)) places the subshell on the left-hand side of `||`, which disables `set -e` (`errexit`) throughout `"$fn"` ([`control_drop_overflow`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh#L138-L152), [`control_lcb_off_by_one`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh#L154-L170), [`control_spec_oracle`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh#L172-L187)).
  In [`emitArtifacts`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.lean#L150-L164), [`writeBackends`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.lean#L157) writes the unmutated `llvm.ll`, `lcb_body.s`, and `lcb_rt.ssa` *before* checking `if changed = original` ([`spec_diff.lean:160`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.lean#L160)) and *before* [`writeOutcome`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.lean#L179) writes `$d/status` and `$d/stderr`. If `drop-overflow-llvm` fails to mutate `llvm.ll`, `bounded 120 "${driver[@]}" control-emit ...` returns `1`, which is ignored because `set -e` is disabled; [`build`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh#L144) then compiles the unmutated files, [`observe`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh#L145) runs `llvm.exe`, and `judge "$d" "$d/llvm"` ([`spec_diff.sh:146`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh#L146)) fails because `$d/status` does not exist. [`control_drop_overflow`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh#L150-L151) then prints the expected `FAIL drop-overflow-llvm:` line and returns `1`, passing [`run_control`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh#L122-L132) vacuously. The same happens in [`control_lcb_off_by_one`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh#L154-L170) and [`control_spec_oracle`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh#L172-L187) if `control-emit` / `control-spec-oracle` fails after `writeBackends`.
- **Non-canonical LCB numbering and unmasked `+ 1` in [`lcbOffByOne`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.lean#L74-L89):**
  [`LCB.term`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/Concrete/Backend/LCB.lean#L159-L163) translates both `.ret a` and `.trap s` to `Source.Terminator.ret`, and LCB's verified first path (`LCB.assemble .aarch64Macos f` in [`writeLcb`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.lean#L31-L32)) requires canonical `(block, phi, instruction)` numbering (`0 .. valueCount - 1`; see [`Concrete/Backend/LCB.lean:55-57`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/Concrete/Backend/LCB.lean#L55-L57)). For 4 of the 5 BIR productions (`wrapped`, `widening`, `twoSites`, `chain`), Block 1 has a `.ret` terminator while Block 2 defines a `phi` (and/or instructions) with ID `< f.valueWidths.size`. [`lcbOffByOne`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.lean#L74-L89) appends an instruction with `destination := next` (`>= f.valueWidths.size`) to Block 1 *before* Block 2's lower-numbered definitions, which breaks canonical order whenever the seed's first exiting program is not `checked`.
  Furthermore, [`lcbOffByOne`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.lean#L82) adds `1` without masking to `0..255`: if the chosen program exits with `255`, `255 + 1 = 256` encodes either trap site 0 or an invalid result word (`abort()`), not an exit status. And [`control_lcb_off_by_one`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh#L162-L169) only checks `! judge`, which passes on `incomplete` or a crash rather than verifying that both legs exited with `(c + 1) % 256` and empty `stderr`/`stdout`.

**Concrete fix:**
- In [`control_drop_overflow`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh#L142), [`control_lcb_off_by_one`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh#L158), and [`control_spec_oracle`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh#L174), guard the `bounded 120 "${driver[@]}" ...` call with `|| { echo "control setup: driver failed" >&2; return 0; }` (or invoke `"$fn"` via `bash -eo pipefail -c`), and in [`emitArtifacts`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.lean#L157-L161) compute and validate the mutated `llvm.ll` before writing backend files.
- In [`lcbOffByOne`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.lean#L74-L89), either renumber all block phis/instructions/operands canonically after inserting the off-by-one instructions (`(a + 1) & 255` on non-trap returns) and assert `f != origF`, or apply the `+ 1` mutation on the BIR return before `LCB.emit` while computing `status`/`stderr` from the unmutated BIR. In [`control_lcb_off_by_one`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh#L162-L169), assert that `$d/lcb.status` and `$d/lcb_eval.status` equal `$(( ($(cat "$d/status") + 1) % 256 ))` and `$d/lcb.stderr`, `$d/lcb_eval.stderr`, `$d/lcb.stdout`, `$d/lcb_eval.stdout` are empty.

