#### 2. [`Concrete/SpecDiffSpecGen.lean:28-55`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/Concrete/SpecDiffSpecGen.lean#L28-L55), [`Concrete/SpecDiffSpecGen.lean:60-75`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/Concrete/SpecDiffSpecGen.lean#L60-L75) — **HIGH**
**`.letLiteral` in [`SpecGen.go`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/Concrete/SpecDiffSpecGen.lean#L38-L56) emits `.add (.var previous) a` (`addLiteral`) while recording `"let_literal"`, and the return weights in [`weightedProductions`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/Concrete/SpecDiffSpecGen.lean#L28-L30) are dead code.**

- In [`SpecGen.go`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/Concrete/SpecDiffSpecGen.lean#L44-L55):
  ```lean
      let (rhs, r₂) :=
        match production with
        | .letCopy => (Slice0.Expr.atom (.var previous), r₁)
        | .addVariable =>
          let (which, r') := below vars.length r₁
          (.add (.var previous) (.var (vars.getD which previous)), r')
        | _ =>
          let (a, r') := literal r₁
          (.add (.var previous) a, r')
  ```
  When `pick statementProductions r` chooses `.letLiteral`, it hits the wildcard `| _ =>` arm and emits `.add (.var previous) a` (an `add_literal` statement, not `let x = <lit>`), while line 55 still records `.letLiteral` (`"let_literal"`) in `productions`.
- [`weightedProductions`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/Concrete/SpecDiffSpecGen.lean#L28-L30) lists `(1, .returnLiteral)` and `(5, .returnVariable)`, but [`statementProductions`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/Concrete/SpecDiffSpecGen.lean#L35-L36) filters both out and nothing else reads those weights; [`generate`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/Concrete/SpecDiffSpecGen.lean#L61-L65) hardcodes `below 6 r` instead.
- [`literal`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/Concrete/SpecDiffSpecGen.lean#L31-L33) only samples `below 32 r` (`0..31`), so literal boundary values (`255`) and out-of-range literals (`>= 256`, `ARITH-2`) are never generated.

**Concrete fix:**
- Give `.letLiteral` its own arm `(Slice0.Expr.atom a, r')` in [`SpecGen.go`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/Concrete/SpecDiffSpecGen.lean#L45) and track unread bindings (or allow `.addVariable` to consume two existing bindings) so multi-literal programs remain accepted by `OWN-5` (`Discharged`).
- Sample return productions using [`weightedProductions`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/Concrete/SpecDiffSpecGen.lean#L28-L30) and widen [`literal`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/Concrete/SpecDiffSpecGen.lean#L31-L33) to cover `0..255` (plus occasional `>= 256` literals to exercise `check` refusals).

