#### 3. [`scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh:34-41`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh#L34-L41), [`scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh:99-120`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh#L99-L120), [`scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh:239-299`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh#L239-L299) — **HIGH**
**Deadline / `INCOMPLETE` handling can turn timeouts into false `FAIL`s (exit `1` or `124`), `lake build` and controls are not properly budgeted, and construct/outcome non-vacuity is checked on generated rather than judged programs.**

- **Timeouts in [`native_one`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh#L99-L120) and `gen-*` exit `1` or `124` instead of `3` (`INCOMPLETE`):**
  1. Line 101 calls `build "$name" "$d/build.log" bounded "$(remaining)" ...` without checking `[ "$(remaining)" -gt 0 ]` (same at line 232 in replay mode). If `$(remaining)` reaches `<= 0` after line 268, `bounded_run` rejects the non-positive timeout with exit `2` and [`build`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/lib/slice0_common.sh#L88-L91) calls `exit 1`. Even if `$(remaining)` is `1`–`2`s and `slice0_native.sh` times out twice (`rc=124`), `build` calls `exit 1`.
  2. At lines 102–111, if `secs=$(remaining)` is small and [`observe`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/lib/slice0_common.sh#L75-L82) times out twice, `observe` writes `incomplete` to `$d/$backend.status`. [`judge`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/lib/slice0_common.sh#L84-L86) then sees a mismatch against expected status `0..255`/`134`, calls [`report_mismatch`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh#L109) (printing bogus regression instructions!), and sets `fail=1`. Because [`slice0_common.sh:27`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/lib/slice0_common.sh#L27) only rewrites `rc=0` to `rc=3` on `BOUNDED_LOG` timeouts, the gate exits `1` (`FAIL`) instead of `3` (`INCOMPLETE`).
- **Time budget vs. cold CI builds and controls:**
  `start=$(date +%s)` and `deadline=$((start + budget))` ([`spec_diff.sh:34-37`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh#L34-L37)) start *before* `source scripts/checks/lib/slice0_common.sh`, which runs `lake build Concrete lean-compiler-backend/lcb`. On a cold GitHub-hosted runner without a Lake cache, building LCB + `Concrete` can consume most or all of `SPEC_DIFF_SECS=600`s before generation even starts. Meanwhile, the 4 controls ([`spec_diff.sh:142-210`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh#L142-L210)) use hardcoded `bounded 120` / `bounded 300` instead of `$(remaining)`.
- **Coverage and vacuity guards check `summary.tsv` (generated) instead of judged programs:**
  [`check_generation`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh#L247-L249) and the `exit`/`trap` vacuity guard ([`spec_diff.sh:250-256`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh#L250-L256)) inspect `summary.tsv` (all 300 generated candidates), not the candidates actually compared in the loop ([`spec_diff.sh:266-275`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh#L266-L275)). If the deadline expires after `SPEC_DIFF_MIN_JUDGED=8` candidates, the gate passes even if those 8 judged candidates contain zero traps (or zero exits) and miss productions/types/ops (`add`, `sub`, `mul`, `u8`, `i8`, `u16`, `i16`), and even though [`genBir`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.lean#L208) already wrote `lcb_eval.status` for all accepted candidates without judging them. Similarly, when `spec_compiled > 0` ([`spec_diff.sh:295-298`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh#L295-L298)), the spec leg only checks `spec_judged -eq 0` (so 1 judged program passes) and runs after the BIR loop can exhaust `$(remaining)`.

**Concrete fix:**
- Compute `start`/`deadline` after `source scripts/checks/lib/slice0_common.sh` (leaving `SLICE0_BUILD_SECS` at its 1800s default for the cold Lake build), and pass `$(remaining)` (checked `> 0`) to the control `bounded` calls.
- In [`native_one`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh#L99-L120), check `[ "$(remaining)" -ge 15 ] || return 2` before `build`, run `bounded "$(remaining)"` without `build`'s unconditional `exit 1` when `bounded_is_incomplete "$rc"` holds (returning `2` so the caller exits `3`), and if `[ "$(cat "$d/$backend.status")" = incomplete ]`, return `2` (`INCOMPLETE`) instead of calling `report_mismatch`.
- Judge `lcb_eval` on all generated candidates, require the judged subset to have non-zero `exit` and `trap` counts and construct coverage (including `add`, `sub`, `mul`, `u8`, `i8`, `u16`, `i16` and [`widening`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/Concrete/SpecDiffBirGen.lean#L94-L101) covering `.u8 -> .i16` as well as `.u8 -> .u16` and `.i8 -> .i16`), and require `[ "$spec_judged" -ge "$minimum_judged" ]` when `spec_compiled > 0`.

