#### 4. [`scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.lean:247-253`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.lean#L247-L253), [`scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh:86-96`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh#L86-L96), [`scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh:225-237`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh#L225-L237) — **MEDIUM**
**[`writeSpecOutcome`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.lean#L247-L253) picks the first site of kind `k` regardless of which site trapped, and [`report_mismatch`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh#L79-L97) on the spec leg prints a replay command that replays the BIR leg instead.**

- In [`writeSpecOutcome`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.lean#L247-L253):
  ```lean
  | .trap k => match p.sites.find? (fun e => e.kind = k) with
    | some e => writeObservation dir "134" (Runtime.trapLine e ++ "\n"); return true
  ```
  When a lowered program has multiple sites of the same trap kind (e.g. two `+` operations both with `.arithmeticOverflow`), `p.sites.find? (fun e => e.kind = k)` always chooses the first entry in `p.sites`, producing the wrong expected trap line whenever a later site traps.
- In [`report_mismatch`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh#L96), a spec-leg failure prints `SPEC_DIFF_REPLAY='$seed:$index' bash scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh`, and also prints `Concrete.BIR.Examples` instructions using `bir:` manifest syntax, while the replay handler ([`spec_diff.sh:225-237`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh#L225-L237) and [`spec_diff.lean:360`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.lean#L360)) exclusively runs [`emitBirCandidate`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.lean#L166-L185) (`BirGen.generate`).

**Concrete fix:**
- In [`writeSpecOutcome`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.lean#L247-L253), refuse `.trap k` when `(p.sites.filter (·.kind = k)).length != 1` until the spec evaluator carries the trapping site identity.
- Add `replay-spec SEED INDEX DIR TARGET` to [`spec_diff.lean`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.lean#L360), accept `SPEC_DIFF_REPLAY=spec:SEED:INDEX` and `bir:SEED:INDEX` (keeping `SEED:INDEX` for BIR) in [`spec_diff.sh:225-237`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh#L225-L237), and print `SPEC_DIFF_REPLAY="$leg:$seed:$index"` in [`report_mismatch`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/ro-A1/scripts/checks/compiler/spec_diff.sh#L96).

